  "notes": "The purest country *power ballad* band of the era. The entry calls this catalogue \"the clearest template in the section for 'the drums *are* the dynamic map,'\" and the stated staging is authored directly: \"verse on hats or cross-stick with kick on 1 and 3, snare and full kit at the chorus, a tom-driven bridge, and a final chorus with crash on every downbeat plus a doubled snare.\" Harmony is quoted as \"textbook I–V–vi–IV and vi–IV–I–V, with a IV–V–I plagal-into-authentic cadence at the end of every chorus\" — the third family is that cadence. The bass device is structural rather than tonal: \"whole and half notes under verses, 8ths under final choruses; bass drop-out for the first four bars of the last chorus then re-entry is a documented-lane device,\" so root-following is high and anticipation stays low while the arrangement does the work. Melody is \"low, narrow verse; chorus leaps to the top of the tenor register and holds,\" with the entry noting the final chorus is often lifted a step or an octave. ⚠ Confidence is medium (research: medium-high); the per-track readings are [LOW-CONF]. ⚠ The INFERRED parameters are the tom/crash perc lanes and density, the velocity spread and the countermelody ratio — \"tom-driven bridge\" and \"crash on every downbeat\" are directions, and 1–4 / 118–127 / 0.4 are this author's reading of them.",
